ighly  valued strava could have helped them  expand to outdoor fitness whoop would  have enabled better health monitoring  tonal would let them offer strength  training and hydros rowing machine seems  like a logical extension from stationary  bikes all of those companies are worth  less than eight billion dollars in total  meanwhile peloton was worth 60 billion  at its peak it's hard to say if that  strategy would have worked out for them  but peloton has fallen in value to just  eight billion dollars today so clearly  shareholders aren't optimistic about  them scaling any further when you're a  public company you need to be able to  consistently find new areas for growth  it's an incredibly challenging task but  that's why these companies are worth  billions but there's an entirely  separate class of companies that are  essentially untouchable they are the  mega corporations that have achieved  startup nirvana and broken through the  sixth and final hurdle of business  success they've created a platform  every startup loves to say that they're  building a platform it's a super trendy  buzzword and to be fair some  entrepreneurs really are building  platforms but these things take time to  actually develop microsoft is the  classic example of a platform business  and bill gates has outlined exactly how  he thinks about building platforms bill  says that you're only really a platform  if the value of the ecosystem on top of  the platform is larger than the company  that owns the platform what that means  in practice is that you're enabling  entirely new businesses to develop on  top of what you've built and if you add  up all the value that those businesses  create it's larger than the underlying  company that's certainly true for  microsoft windows which has enabled  entire industries to flourish everything  from accounting software to video games  is built on top of windows but microsoft  isn't the only platform company out  there every major tech company has  figured out a way to conquer level 6 and  become a platform apple has the iphone  and mac platform amazon has built a  platform for independent merchants and  tons of businesses have been built on  top of google search google apps and  even youtube so regardless of where you  are in these six stages of business  growth just stay focused on getting to  the next level and if you'd like to  learn about how shopify grew from a tiny  snowboarding website into a  multi-billion dollar e-commerce platform  just watch this video next thanks for  watching

